| order by ['Billable GB'] desc","size":0,"title":"Custom collection billable GB by table (what to bill for in LAW)","timeContextFromParameter":"TimeRange","queryType":0,"resourceType":"microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces","showExportToExcel":true,"gridSettings":{"filter":true,"rowLimit":10000,"formatters":[{"columnMatch":"Billable GB","formatter":4,"formatOptions":{"palette":"green","min":0}},{"columnMatch":"Avg GB per day","formatter":4,"formatOptions":{"palette":"blue","min":0}}]}},"customWidth":"50","name":"ov-custom-ingest-grid"}]},"conditionalVisibility":{"parameterName":"Tab","comparison":"isEqualTo","value":"Overview"},"name":"group-overview"},{"type":12,"content":{"version":"NotebookGroup/1.0","groupType":"editable","items":[{"type":1,"content":{"json":"### Process events
**Threat use case:** LOLBins, suspicious child processes, credential theft command lines, discovery commands. Default `DeviceProcessEvents` already captures process creation, so the uplift here is smaller. The value of custom collection is capturing process activity the default sensor sampling may drop under load.  
**Action types (rule wizard):** `ProcessCreated`. One action type per rule, required single select. Your rule streams `ProcessCreated`.  
**Rule conditions:** conditions are AND filters that narrow volume, not extra fields. One or two is normal. Hard cap is 75,000 events per rule per device per 24h rolling window, past which the rule stops streaming until the window resets."},"name":"pr-header"},{"type":3,"content":{"version":"KqlItem/1.0","query":"let cd = DeviceCustomProcessEvents | where Timestamp {TimeRange} | distinct DeviceName;
