**Threat use case:** C2 beaconing, exfil to rare destinations, lateral movement, DNS and TLS to newly seen domains. Default `DeviceNetworkEvents` is heavily curated. Custom collection captures far more connection events, which is why the volume uplift here is large.  
**Action types (rule wizard):** `KerberosConnectionInspected`, `ConnectionSuccess`, `ListeningConnectionCreated`, `NetworkSignatureInspected`, `SshConnectionInspected`, `SmtpConnectionInspected`, `FtpConnectionInspected`, `IcmpConnectionInspected`, `HttpConnectionInspected`, `SslConnectionInspected`, `DnsConnectionInspected`, `NtlmAuthenticationInspected`, `InboundInternetScanInspected`, `ConnectionAttempt`, `ConnectionAcknowledged`, `ConnectionFailed`, `InboundConnectionAccepted`, and additional connection action types below the fold. One action type per rule, required single select. Your rule streams `ConnectionSuccess`. C2 and beacon hunts often also want `ConnectionAttempt` and `ConnectionFailed`, each its own rule.  
**Rule conditions:** conditions are AND filters that narrow volume, not extra fields. One or two is normal. Hard cap is 75,000 events per rule per device per 24h rolling window, past which the rule stops streaming until the window resets."},"name":"nw-header"},{"type":3,"content":{"version":"KqlItem/1.0","query":"let cd = DeviceCustomNetworkEvents | where Timestamp {TimeRange} | distinct DeviceName;
